@startuml

title Restoring the feeds when the synthetic service starts

hide footbox
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left

participant "Synthetic service" as syn
database "Feed configs" as db
participant "IAM" as iam
participant "Marketdata" as md

syn -> db : list the active tenants
loop each tenant, the system tenant first
    syn -> db : read the collections and feeds\nin the tenant, through its root party
    loop each feed with enabled and auto_start
        alt the collection holds a run grant
            syn -> iam : iam.v1.ops.exchange_run_grant(grant id, run id)\nAuthorization: the service's own token
            iam --> syn : run token, or refused (grant lapsed)
        end
        alt a token is held, or the feed has a fixed price
            syn -> md : read the vintage series and observations\nAuthorization: the run token
            syn -> syn : start the feed
        else the feed starts from a vintage and has no token
            syn -> syn : skip the feed and log the reason
        end
    end
end

note over syn
    A restart uses the same exchange as the Start command.
    No person is present, so the stored consent stands in for the operator.
    A restore creates no binding: the stored bindings stand.
end note

@enduml
